-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/1ab3d86f-e14c-4b83-a319-340c8adb8156
-- title:
--   Probability model: i.i.d. rounds $((V^{\mathrm{sell}}_t,V^{\mathrm{buy}}_t),U_t)\sim\mathcal V\otimes\mathrm{Unif}[0,1]$, and the filtration $\mathcal F_t$
-- statement:
--   A **market** on a probability space $(\Omega,\mathbb P)$ is a triple of real sequences: the seller valuations $V^{\mathrm{sell}}_t$, the buyer valuations $V^{\mathrm{buy}}_t$ and uniform draws $U_t$ that the algorithm uses for its randomized corrections. The **probability model** with valuation law $\mathcal V$ requires that
--
--   1. every $V^{\mathrm{sell}}_t$, $V^{\mathrm{buy}}_t$, $U_t$ is measurable;
--   2. the round vectors $W_t=((V^{\mathrm{sell}}_t,V^{\mathrm{buy}}_t),U_t)$ are mutually independent;
--   3. each $W_t$ has law $\mathcal V\otimes\mathrm{Unif}[0,1]$.
--
--   So the valuation pairs are i.i.d. from $\mathcal V$, with arbitrary correlation inside a round, and $U_t$ is uniform and independent of the round's valuations and of the past. The **filtration** is
--   $$
--   \mathcal F_t=\sigma(W_1,\dots,W_t),\qquad \mathcal F_0=\{\emptyset,\Omega\},
--   $$
--   generated by all valuations and algorithmic random draws through round $t$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The sequences are indexed by $\mathbb N$; round $t\in[T]=\{1,\dots,T\}$ uses index $t$, and index $0$ is unused. A Bernoulli draw $X\sim\mathrm{Bern}(p)$ of Algorithm 4 is realized as $X=\mathbb 1\{U_t<p\}$; at most one such draw is made per round.
-- source:
--   Maran, Restelli, Stradi, No-Regret Revenue Maximization in Sequential Market Making Under Inventory Constraints, arXiv:2610.24562v1, Sec. 3, p. 14; Algorithm 4, p. 37; proofs of Proposition 6.12, p. 42, and Theorem 6.18, p. 47

import Mathlib

namespace InvMarketMaking.LOB

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

/-- The random inputs of the market: round `t` (for `t ≥ 1`) brings the seller valuation `Vs t`, the
buyer valuation `Vb t`, and the algorithm's fresh uniform draw `U t` (Maran, Restelli, Stradi,
arXiv:2610.24562v1, Sec. 3, p. 14, and Algorithm 4, p. 37).

**Formalization Note** The family is indexed by `ℕ`; round `t ∈ [T] = {1, …, T}` uses index `t`,
and index `0` (and every index beyond the horizon) is an unused extra draw. -/
structure Market (Ω : Type*) where
  /-- seller valuation `V^sell_t` -/
  Vs : ℕ → Ω → ℝ
  /-- buyer valuation `V^buy_t` -/
  Vb : ℕ → Ω → ℝ
  /-- the uniform draw `U_t` realizing the Bernoulli corrections of Algorithm 4 -/
  U : ℕ → Ω → ℝ

/-- The uniform law on `[0, 1]`. -/
noncomputable def unif01 : Measure ℝ := volume.restrict (Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) 1)

/-- The probability model of the maker–takers interaction (arXiv:2610.24562v1, Sec. 3, p. 14):
the round variables `W_t = ((V^sell_t, V^buy_t), U_t)` are measurable, mutually independent across
rounds, and each has law `V ⊗ Unif[0,1]`. So the valuation pairs are i.i.d. from the unknown joint
law `V` (the two coordinates arbitrarily correlated within a round), and the algorithm's draw `U_t`
is uniform and independent of the round's valuations and of the past.

**Formalization Note** The paper writes "Sample `X ∼ Bern(p)`" in Algorithm 4 (Lines 11, 16); this
is realized as `X = 1{U_t < p}`. At most one of the two Bernoulli draws is made per round, so one
`U_t` per round suffices. -/
def IsRoundModel {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (P : Measure Ω) (V : Measure (ℝ × ℝ))
    (M : Market Ω) : Prop :=
  (∀ t, Measurable (M.Vs t) ∧ Measurable (M.Vb t) ∧ Measurable (M.U t)) ∧
  iIndepFun (fun t ω => ((M.Vs t ω, M.Vb t ω), M.U t ω)) P ∧
  ∀ t, HasLaw (fun ω => ((M.Vs t ω, M.Vb t ω), M.U t ω)) (V.prod unif01) P

/-- The σ-algebra `ℱ_t` generated by all valuations and algorithmic random draws through round
`t`, i.e. by `W_1, …, W_t` with `W_s = ((V^sell_s, V^buy_s), U_s)`; `ℱ_0` is trivial
(arXiv:2610.24562v1, proofs of Proposition 6.12, p. 42, and Theorem 6.18, p. 47). -/
@[instance_reducible]
noncomputable def roundSigma {Ω : Type*} (M : Market Ω) (t : ℕ) : MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  ⨆ s ∈ Finset.Icc 1 t,
    MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω => ((M.Vs s ω, M.Vb s ω), M.U s ω)) inferInstance

end InvMarketMaking.LOB


